.TH HISTORY 3 "February 2026" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
history_init, history_end, history \- editline history management interface
.SH LIBRARY
Editline library (libedit, \-ledit)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <histedit.h>
.PP
.B typedef struct history History;
.PP
.B typedef struct hist_event {
.br
.BI "    int num;"
.br
.BI "    const char *str;"
.br
.B } HistEvent;
.PP
.BI "History *history_init(void);"
.br
.BI "void history_end(History *h);"
.br
.BI "int history(History *h, HistEvent *ev, int op, ...);"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR history_init ()
creates a history state object.
.BR history_end ()
releases that object.
.PP
.BR history ()
performs commands selected by
.I op
and optionally reports results in
.IR ev .
.PP
Public operation macros are:
.TP
.B H_ENTER
Add a new history entry.
.TP
.B H_APPEND
Append text to the current entry.
.TP
.B H_PREV
Move to the previous entry.
.TP
.B H_NEXT
Move to the next entry.
.TP
.B H_CURR
Read the current entry.
.TP
.B H_FIRST
Move to the first entry.
.TP
.B H_LAST
Move to the most recent entry.
.TP
.B H_SET
Select an entry by absolute history index.
.TP
.B H_CLEAR
Clear the history list.
.TP
.B H_LOAD
Load history from a file.
The file must have been written by
.BR H_SAVE .
Each line in the file represents one history entry.
If the file does not exist or cannot be opened, the operation fails.
.TP
.B H_SAVE
Save all history entries to a file.
Entries are written one per line in order from oldest to newest.
The resulting file can later be passed to
.BR H_LOAD
to restore session history.
.TP
.B H_SETSIZE
Set maximum number of history entries.
.TP
.B H_GETSIZE
Get maximum number of history entries.
.TP
.B H_SETUNIQUE
Enable or disable duplicate suppression.
.TP
.B H_GETUNIQUE
Get duplicate suppression state.
.TP
.B H_END
End traversal/search state.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR history_init ()
returns a valid
.B History
pointer on success, or NULL on error.
.PP
.BR history ()
returns 0 on success and \-1 on error.
.BR history_end ()
returns no value.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
Invalid operation or arguments.
.TP
.B ENOMEM
Memory allocation failed.
.TP
.B ENOENT
No matching entry found.
.TP
.B ERANGE
Requested history index is out of range.
.TP
.B EIO
Load/save operation failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
The following program creates a history list, adds an entry, and reads it back:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
#include <histedit.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int
main(void)
{
    History *h = history_init();
    HistEvent ev;

    history(h, &ev, H_SETSIZE, 100);
    history(h, &ev, H_ENTER, "first command");
    if (history(h, &ev, H_FIRST) == 0)
        printf("entry %d: %s\en", ev.num, ev.str);
    history_end(h);
    return 0;
}
.EE
.RE
